From: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: reparse flowtable devices on topology updates

Handle the netifd IFUPDATE_TOPOLOGY event so bridge membership changes
refresh hardware flow offload devices without a full firewall reload.

Signed-off-by: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/root/etc/hotplug.d/iface/20-firewall
+++ b/root/etc/hotplug.d/iface/20-firewall
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 }
 
 [ "$ACTION" = ifup -o "$ACTION" = ifupdate ] || exit 0
-[ "$ACTION" = ifupdate -a -z "$IFUPDATE_ADDRESSES" -a -z "$IFUPDATE_DATA" ] && exit 0
+[ "$ACTION" = ifupdate -a -z "$IFUPDATE_ADDRESSES" -a -z "$IFUPDATE_DATA" -a -z "$IFUPDATE_TOPOLOGY" ] && exit 0
 
 /etc/init.d/firewall enabled || exit 0
 
